\par                               EXPLANATORY NOTES\par
                               ================\par
\par      The tubesheet can be subjected to pressure load applied both on the channel side
\par and on the shell side. The flanged extension of the tubesheet applies on the central
\par part of the latter a bending moment which is added to the effect of the pressure. For
\par these reasons it is necessary to define a sign convention in order to combine cor-
\par rectly the effects of the different load components.
\par      The program AsmeVip defines the following sign convention:
\par The pressures and the flange moments (or equivalent bolt pressures) are positive (ne-
\par gative) when they have the effect to bow the tubesheet with the convex side toward the
\par shell (channel).\par 
